cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  censored-demand-tsfm: reproduction package for "Forecasting for perishable
  replenishment under demand censoring: an evaluation of time series foundation
  models"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying
  paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ahn
    given-names: Suho
    affiliation: >-
      School of Business and Technology Management, Korea Advanced Institute of
      Science and Technology (KAIST), Daejeon, Republic of Korea
    email: dkstngh3502@kaist.ac.kr
repository-code: "https://github.com/suhoahn-web/censored-demand-tsfm"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction package for a study of time series foundation models applied to
  censored fresh-retail demand. Five pre-trained models are crossed with three
  censoring treatments and three adaptation strategies, and every forecast is
  carried through to an order-up-to replenishment decision in a
  perishable-inventory simulation with shelf life, first-in-first-out issuing
  and waste, so that methods are compared by inventory cost as well as by
  forecast error. Includes experiment scripts, evaluation metrics, the inventory
  simulator, significance tests, figure and table generators, and per-run
  metadata recording checkpoint hashes, seeds and library versions.
keywords:
  - demand forecasting
  - censored demand
  - time series foundation models
  - inventory management
  - perishable retail
  - probabilistic forecasting
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
